  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Expressed as a fraction in its simplest form or as an integer, $\\frac{1}{8}÷\\frac{1}{40}=${{field-1}}.",
  "worked_solution": "Dividing a fraction by another fraction is equivalent to multiplying the first fraction by the reciprocal of the second fraction.\n\nThe reciprocal of $\\frac{1}{40}$ is $\\frac{40}{1}.$ So we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{8}÷\\frac{1}{40}=\\frac{1}{8}\\times \\frac{40}{1}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we multiply fractions. We multiply the numerators, and we multiply the denominators:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{8}\\times \\frac{40}{1}=\\frac{1\\times 40}{8\\times 1}=\\frac{40}{8}\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n40÷8=5\n$$",
